From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Storage Maintainers <26684313+sluongng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] storage: Preserve existing recovery files

An application may need to validate a recovered namespace before any
repair or cleanup occurs. Opening an incomplete tree must not create
a replacement, and a later validation failure must not remove orphaned
versions, tables or blob files.

Add a default-off preservation option for existing recovery. Require an
existing current manifest and required directories, and leave recovery
cleanup to a later ordinary open. This option does not make a tree
a read-only API; its database owner controls when writes become allowed.

Reserve table and blob identifiers above all retained files, not just
those referenced by the current version. This prevents resumed writes
from colliding with or overwriting crash orphans. Reject exhausted
IDs without changing files. Ordinary recovery and allocation remain
unchanged.

---
